  "description": "What: the scene of the 3-D map's night-vision and thermal views (CE-1984 / CE-1985; docs/designs/sensor-view/DESIGN_Sensor_View.md \u00a77; mockup docs/UX/sensor-view.svg) \u2014 every heat and light source the views draw, made by the SIMULATION, at night. On basic-desert at 00:30 local, clear sky: 'Idling Tank' (a crewed T-72, Neutral) idles at (450, 200); 'Parked Tank' (a T-72 authored HeatSource Off) stands cold at (450, 300); 'Lit Car' (a crewed HMMWV) at (350, 120) has its lamps on (dark, engine idling); 'Man' stands at (300, 250); 'Leaving Tank' (a crewed T-72) idles at (200, 450) and at 75 s the 'Drive Off' trigger sends it north \u2014 it leaves a warm ground heat mark; 'Gunner' (a friendly M1) kills 'Wreck', a hostile T-72 240 m north of it, whose hull then burns. Everything but the Wreck is Neutral, so the Gunner shoots only it. Judge: the idling tank Idle and the parked one never warm; the car's lamps on; the man a warm body (Standing); the wreck destroyed and burning (FireState); one vehicle-stand heat mark where the Leaving Tank stood. The VIEWS are judged by SensorViewFrameRail (frame rails), not here. Fail: any source missing. Red-proof: author the Parked Tank Idle and it reads warm.",
